<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest. Required on upload since May 2024; without it App Store Connect
  rejects the build after processing, which looks like a successful upload followed by an
  email an hour later.

  TWO CLAIMS ARE MADE HERE AND BOTH HAVE TO BE TRUE:

  1. NSPrivacyTracking false. Voiid does not track — there is no advertising identifier, no
     third-party analytics SDK, and nothing is linked to data from other companies' apps.
     Setting this true would additionally require NSPrivacyTrackingDomains.

  2. NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes. UserDefaults is a "required reason" API. CA92.1 is the
     reason for "access info from same app, per documentation" — this app reads and writes
     only its own preferences, never another app's via an app group with a wider audience.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED. Contacts, photos, location, camera and microphone are
  covered by the Info.plist usage strings and by App Store Connect's own privacy
  questionnaire, not by this file. NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is the field for those and it
  is left absent rather than guessed at: an inaccurate collection declaration is worse than
  the questionnaire, because the questionnaire is reviewed and this is not.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
